  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A planet having mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></msub></math>&nbsp;and radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></msub><mo>,</mo></math> where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></msub></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></msub></math>&nbsp;are mass and radius of earth respectively, has escape velocity in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>km</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> given by:&nbsp;(Given escape velocity on earth <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>V</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>)</p>",
    "image": null
